---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SubscribeForm from "../components/SubscribeForm.astro";
import { meta, sections } from "../data";
---

<Base title={meta.home.title} description={meta.home.description} canonical="/">
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">Capital, ownership and control for MENA founders.</p>
    <h1>Understand what your next round changes.</h1>
    <p>A financing round changes your ownership, the decisions you can make, and what you receive when the company is sold. Its terms also shape the next round.</p>
    <p>MENADD helps founders compare financing proposals, model dilution across successive rounds, understand investor rights with counsel, and prepare alternatives if the capital plan changes. For cross-border companies, we also examine the structure the financing needs to work through.</p>
    <p>Start with the decision in front of you: a term sheet, a new convertible instrument, a bridge, or the next priced round.</p>
    <div class="assessment-cta-group">
      <a class="button-link" href="/financing-terms/#start">Discuss your financing decision</a>
      <a class="quiet-link" href="/library/">Explore the diligence library</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>When to work with MENADD</h2>
    <div class="assessment-chooser">
      <a class="assessment-choice" href="/financing-terms/#financing-terms">
        <h2>You have financing terms to evaluate</h2>
        <p>Compare the proposed terms, model their financial consequences and prepare the issues you want to negotiate before signing.</p>
        <p>See the work</p>
      </a>
      <a class="assessment-choice" href="/financing-terms/#ownership-and-control">
        <h2>You need to see beyond this round</h2>
        <p>Model existing instruments, new investment and option pools together. See how ownership, control and exit distributions change through later financings.</p>
        <p>See the work</p>
      </a>
      <a class="assessment-choice" href="/financing-terms/#next-financing">
        <h2>The capital plan has changed</h2>
        <p>Compare additional funding, bridge and down-round scenarios, including the dilution, consent requirements and implications for the next financing.</p>
        <p>See the work</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Checks you can run before a conversation</h2>
    <div class="assessment-chooser">
      <a class="assessment-choice" href="/assessment/structure/">
        <h2>Structure and ownership</h2>
        <p>Check the ownership record, employee equity and entity structure behind your financing.</p>
        <p>Run the structure check</p>
      </a>
      <a class="assessment-choice" href="/assessment/">
        <h2>Financial metrics</h2>
        <p>See the questions your recurring or repeatable B2B revenue metrics may raise during investor diligence.</p>
        <p>Run the financial check</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Library Sections</h2>
    <div class="section-list">
      {
        sections.map((section) => (
          <div class="section-entry">
            <h3><a href={section.href}>{section.title}</a></h3>
            <p>{section.short}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why "built from the diligence backwards"</h2>
    <p>A standard diligence process starts from the investor and works into the company. This library runs the same route in reverse: it starts from the questions diligence will ask and works back to how the company should have been built.</p>
    <p>The same logic applies to the structure itself. It should be designed from the capital stack backwards. Before the first entity is opened. Not after the first term sheet.</p>
    <p>The material comes from operating experience, not theory. A decade inside venture-backed companies, on the founder and CFO side of the table, in the UAE and across borders.</p>
    <a class="cta-link" href="/about/">About →</a>
  </section>

  <SubscribeForm sourcePage="/" />
</Base>
